From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:24:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 22/30] CREDITS: the DroidVM pseudo-unprotected mode and boot
 shim

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 CREDITS | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CREDITS b/CREDITS
index 79ccf8b..c50f3a4 100644
--- a/CREDITS
+++ b/CREDITS
@@ -19,3 +19,9 @@ Upstream crosvm files stay under their BSD-3-Clause license (LICENSE).
   header. Links the system LibVNCServer (GPL-2.0-or-later). The option wiring (src/crosvm/config.rs
   VncConfig, cmdline.rs, sys/linux/gpu.rs, simplefb_display.rs, devices DisplayBackend::Vnc) is our own,
   modelled on DroidVM's.
+- DroidVM dvm-crosvm 849e05f, same licence: the pseudo-unprotected memory mode ("--protected-vm-pseudo-unprotected",
+  iceland-vms 0.2-11 "Shared with the tablet") -- droidvm-shim/ (the boot shim, kept with its own headers as
+  published) and hypervisor/src/gunyah/shim_abi.rs (the host / shim ABI, kept as published); the crosvm side
+  (aarch64/src/lib.rs layout + load_shim / init_handoff, hypervisor/src/gunyah/mod.rs window share + watch_shim,
+  vm_memory SharedGuestRam / ShimHandoff, the cmdline flag) follows DroidVM's design and is re-plumbed onto our
+  host kernel's GH_VM_PROTECTED_SHARE (patch 0008) instead of DroidVM's out-of-tree share module.
